Apple this week <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ios-27-features-to-try-first/">released iOS 27</a> following around three months of beta testing. If you just installed the software update on your iPhone, you might be wondering where the new-and-improved Siri AI and dedicated Siri app are. In case you missed it, you must join Apple's waitlist in order to gain access to these new features.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/Personalized-Siri-iOS-27.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="895" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1051121" /><br/>
Keep in mind that while iOS 27 is compatible with the iPhone 11 and newer, Siri AI is limited to the iPhone 15 Pro and newer. This is because Siri AI requires an iPhone model that is compatible with Apple Intelligence, which we have listed below.<br/>
<br/>
Fortunately, joining the Siri AI waitlist is a simple task:<ul><br/>
  <li>Open the <strong>Settings app</strong> on your iPhone.</li><br/>
  <li>Tap on the <strong>Siri menu</strong>.</li><br/>
  <li>Tap on <strong>Try Siri AI (Beta)</strong>.</li><br/>
  <li>Follow the prompts.</li><br/>
</ul>Wait times seem to vary, with some users receiving access to Siri AI within a few minutes of signing up and others having to wait a few hours or even days.<br/>
<br/>
You will receive a notification on your iPhone once you have received access to Siri AI, and the Siri app will automatically appear on your device at that time. You can talk or type to Siri AI in three ways: swipe down on your iPhone's Dynamic Island, press and hold your iPhone's side button to invoke the assistant, or open the Siri app.<br/>
<br/>
The classic version of Siri has always been useful for basic actions like setting a timer and checking the weather, but it has notoriously struggled with more advanced requests over the years. Siri AI is much more intelligent and personalized: it is essentially a ChatGPT-like version of Siri that can respond to most questions.<br/>
<br/>
Siri AI can draw on your personal information stored on your iPhone, has on-screen awareness, and can perform actions in more apps that support it.<br/>
<br/>
The new Siri is limited to English to start, but Apple said support for French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, and Spanish will be available in October, likely as part of the release of iOS 27.1. Apple said Siri AI has unspecified daily usage limits, but it noted that expanded access will be coming with select iCloud+ plans.<br/>
<br/>
Siri AI is not available in the EU on iOS 27, iPadOS 27, and watchOS 27 at launch, as Apple is in a regulatory battle with the European Commission.<br/>
